        'Players bet; each receives three tiles and arranges them in a line to form top and bottom hand (totals mod 10). Tiles placed face-down. Banker exposes three tiles and arranges similarly. Compare: player top vs banker top, player bottom vs banker bottom. Both player hands win or one wins and one ties = player wins even money; one wins one loses = push; otherwise player loses. Banker wins ties.',
